{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening fee cap and refund rules","requirement":"A landlord may charge an application screening fee only up to actual out-of-pocket costs and never more than $30 per applicant; no fee may be charged when no unit is available; a receipt is required and unused amounts must be refunded.","key_value":"$30 per applicant, CPI-adjustable each year","coverage_conditions":"Applicants for residential rental property, including guarantors or cosigners; 'landlord' means an owner of residential rental property. Applies when a landlord or agent receives a request to rent and charges a screening fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property"},"exemptions":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules on deposits and fees; the fee is not an 'advance fee' or 'security'; a landlord may accept a reusable screening report under Section 1950.1.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant.","interaction":"Section is not intended to preempt federal or state housing assistance program regulations governing collection of deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California order-of-consideration rule for rental applications","requirement":"A landlord charging a screening fee must give screening criteria in writing with the application, consider completed applications in the order received, and approve the first applicant who meets the criteria.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Landlords or their agents charging an application screening fee on residential rental property; the process is offered as a condition of charging that fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property"},"exemptions":"No refund owed to an applicant denied after consideration for failing the criteria; inadvertent concurrent-application fee collections are excused if refunded within seven days. Alternative: return the entire fee within 7 days of selecting a tenant or 30 days of application, whichever is first.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
